{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<?ui-args --service-package tests/ui/service-events/reply.service.json?>\n<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\"\n       xmlns:event=\"https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event\"\n       version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"waiting\">\n  <state id=\"waiting\">\n    <invoke type=\"urn:example:reply\" id=\"reply\"/>\n    <transition event=\"reply.ready\" target=\"done\" event:schema='{\"type\":\"string\"}'/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml095-service-event-schema.scxml"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml095-service-event-schema.scxml"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":19,"byteOffset":398,"endColumn":83,"endLine":7,"startColumn":64,"startLine":7},"insertedContent":{"text":"'{\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}'"}}]}],"description":{"text":"use the schema the package declares for `reply.ready`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml095-service-event-schema.scxml"},"region":{"endColumn":82,"endLine":7,"startColumn":65,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"this `event:schema` is not the schema the service package declares for `reply.ready`\n\n**Note:** the service package of `urn:example:reply` declares that it emits `reply.ready` with the schema sha256:e3dce8d1afb8 (`{\"properties\":{\"text\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"text\"],\"type\":\"object\"}`); a transition that handles the event while the service runs describes the same data, so its schema must be that one (canonical JSON, compared exactly) or `true`\n\n**Help:** use the package's schema for the event, or correct the service package if the document is right\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>","text":"this `event:schema` is not the schema the service package declares for `reply.ready`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":416,"start":399},"category":"package"},"ruleId":"SCXML095"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"a service package may declare the events its invoked service emits, each with a JSON Schema for the event's data (`events.emits`); a transition in the state that invokes the service, or in a descendant of it, that names such an event exactly describes the same data, so its `event:schema` must be the package's schema, compared as canonical JSON, or the boolean schema `true`. Reported only for the service packages the validator was given; `event:schemaexpr`, prefix descriptors, and `<invoke typeexpr>` are not judged. The document's schema stays metadata only: the session host enforces the package's contract itself"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: use the package's schema for the event (the `maybe-incorrect` fix), or correct the service package when the document is right.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §6.4 <invoke>\n\nRun `scxml-cli --explain SCXML095` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#invoke","id":"SCXML095","name":"SCXML095","properties":{"category":"package"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a transition's `event:schema` differs from the schema a bound service package declares for the event"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}